    "https://careersmanager.pageuppeople.com/873/sm/en-us/Search/?search-keyword=&work-type=instructional+faculty+-+temporary%2flecturer%2cinstructional+faculty+%e2%80%93+tenured%2ftenure-track&subscribe=true": {
      "title": "CSUSM Recruitment",
      "description": "CSUSM Recruitment - Search Results skip to main content skip to navigation skip to current link Site Menu Job Opportunities Staff and Management Careers Faculty Careers CSUSM Corporation Careers Student Employment Pay and Benefits Benefits Portal Employment and Compensation About About San Marcos skip to main content skip to section navigation CSUSM Recruitment Job Opportunities Pay and Benefits About Staff and Management Careers Faculty Careers CSUSM Corporation Careers Student Employment Benefits Portal Employment and Compensation About San Marcos CSUSM Recruitment Great Minds Doing Great Work EXISTING APPLICANT LOGIN Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Open Date Close Date Lecturer Pool - Computer Science and Information Systems: Cybersecurity AY 2026/27 San Marcos September 01, 2026 May 31, 2027 The Department of Computer Science and Information Systems at California State University San Marcos accepts applications on an on-going basis for our pool of part-time lecturers for Masters in Cybersecurity Program. Applicant pools are used to fill short-term temporary Lecturer positions across our campus with the possibility of rehiring. Appointments may last from one day to a whole semester. This applicant pool may be used to fill vacant positions on an as-needed basis throughout the academic year.  Applications in this pool ad will only be good for the current academic year. This pool will be closed effective May 31st.  If you wish to be considered for the next academic year, you will need to apply to the new pool as it becomes available by June 15th. MBA Research Assistant San Marcos August 05, 2026 May 31, 2027 The CoBA MBA Program is seeking Research Assistants for the 2026-2027 academic year to support several faculty-led research projects in areas related to business, organizations, technology, education, and professional success. Lecturer - SPAN 101: Beginning Spanish I (Fall 2026) San Marcos August 05, 2026 The Modern Language Studies Department at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach SPAN 101: Beginning Spanish I. The course is an introduction to the Spanish language and Spanish-speaking cultures, with emphasis on the development of communicative skills and grammatical structures. Language laboratory practice is a mandatory component of the course. Lecturer AY- KINE 336: Nutrition for Health & Exercise Performance and KINE 416: Global Nutrition and Health Practices (Fall 2026) San Marcos August 04, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Kinesiology at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for the Fall 2026 semester to teach courses in nutrition including KINE 336: Nutrition for Health and Exercise Performance and KINE 416: Global Nutrition and Health Practices. These courses are taught as part of the kinesiology major and the minor in nutrition. The interdisciplinary minor in Nutrition provides students with an understanding of the role that food and nutrition play in health, nutrition policy, disease prevention, and the science of nutrition. Coursework includes topics in nutrition and wellness, metabolism, life-cycle nutrition, sports nutrition, cultural aspects of food, and current nutrition topics. Lecturer - MUSC 311: Advanced Recording Techniques (Fall 2026) San Marcos August 03, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Music seeks a lecturer to teach Audio Recording Technology.  The lecturer is responsible for teaching an advanced digital audio recording course with an emphasis on professional studio recording techniques, Pro Tools, microphones, signal flow, mixing, mastering, and digital audio production. The instructor will provide students with hands-on training in a professional recording studio environment while integrating lecture, demonstrations, and collaborative lab activities. This course is designed as a seminar/lab with applied learning at its core. The successful candidate will foster an engaging, industry-focused classroom that emphasizes attendance, participation, critical listening, technical proficiency, and creative problem-solving. Lecturer - SPAN 102: Beginning Spanish II (Fall 2026) San Marcos August 03, 2026 The Modern Language Studies Department at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach SPAN 102: Beginning Spanish II. This course is a continuation of SPAN 101. Further study of the Spanish language and Spanish-speaking cultures, with emphasis on the development of communicative skills and basic structures. Lecturer - MATH 103: Supported Finite Mathematics and Algebra (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Mathematics at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach Math 103 - Supported Finite Mathematics and Algebra.  The course covers finite mathematics with integrated review of intermediate algebra. Examines graphs, equations, inequalities, and functions (linear, quadratic, exponential, logarithm), basic probability, data descriptions, and measures of central tendency and dispersion. Intended as a mathematical foundation for students not on a track to take calculus. Lecture - MSW 540:  Field Instruction I (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Social Work at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for fall 2026 to teach MSW 540 Field Instruction I. MSW 540 is the first course of a foundation two-semester sequence. Supervised practice in a social services or related agency developing basic micro, mezzo, and macro skills with an emphasis on culturally informed social work practice. Field seminar and 16 hours weekly supervised agency field experience. Graded Credit/ No Credit. Lecturer Pool - Department of Social Work AY 2026/27 San Marcos July 20, 2026 May 31, 2027 The Department of Social Work at California State University San Marcos accepts applications on an ongoing basis for our pool of part-time lecturers. Salary is commensurate with credentials and experience. Applicant pools are used to fill short-term temporary Lecturer positions across our campus with the possibility of rehiring. Appointments may last from one day to a whole semester. This applicant pool may be used to fill vacant positions on an as-needed basis throughout the academic year.  Applications in this pool ad will only be good for the current academic year. This pool will be closed effective May 31st.  If you wish to be considered for the next academic year, you will need to apply to the new pool as it becomes available by June 15th. Lecturer - MSW 510: Generalist Practice I: Individuals (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Social Work at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer to teach MSW 510- Generalist Practice I: Individuals. The course addresses generalist social work practice with diverse individuals within a person-in-environment perspective. Emphasizes core social work knowledge, values, and skills within the context of evidence informed engagement, assessment, intervention, and evaluation. Lecturer - ANTH 240: Intro to Biological Anthropology (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Anthropology at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach ANTH-240 Introduction to Biological Anthropology. The course introduces students to the subfield of anthropology that examines human origins, evolution, biological variation, and adaptability. Topics include the basic principles of genetics and inheritance, evolutionary theory, primate biology and behavior, the fossil record of human and nonhuman primates, and contemporary human biological diversity. Lecturer - GES 102: Matter, Molecules, Life, and the Environment II (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture GES 102: Matter, Molecules, Life and the Environment II. The course is the second of a two-semester course consisting of integrated modules covering the areas of matter/energy, molecules, living systems, and environment. These modules will cover major concepts in the physical and biological sciences, emphasizing their application to real-world problems. Concepts covered will include the interactions of matter and energy, laws of motion, atomic structure of matter, structure and properties of molecules, principles of genetics, structure and function of living organisms, evolution, and interactions of organisms with each other and their environment. Includes practical experience in the application of the scientific method through laboratory activities. Lecturer - BIOL 104: Priciples of Biology: Human Emphasis  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 104: Principles of Biology: Human Emphasis. The course teaches the principles of cellular, organismal and population biology with primary representation relating to the human organism. Includes study of cells, tissues, and mammalian organ systems. Lecturer - BIOL 212: Evolution  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 212: Evolution. The course is a consideration of evolution as the unifying concept in biology. Diversity and adaptation of form, function, and behavior of living organisms. Biological, geological, anthropological, and chemical evidence for and mechanisms of evolutionary change, including global pattern of distribution and specialization, mass extinctions, the evolution of race and sex, and the origin of species. Lecturer - BIOL 215: Experimental Design & Statistical Analysis  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 215: Experimental Design and Statistical Analysis. The course teaches the design and analysis of biological surveys and experiments. Includes hypothesis formation, experimental design, statistical analysis, presentation of results, and hands-on experience in design and analysis of biological experiments. Lecturer - BIOL 354: Principles of Ecology  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 354: Principles of Ecology. The course is a discussion of major concepts in population, community, and evolutionary ecology including population growth and regulation, competition, predation, energetics, adaptations, and diversity. Lecturer - MSW 661: Social Work in Health Care (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 16, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Social Work at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer to teach MSW 661- Social Work in Healthcare. The course covers the roles and responsibilities of social workers as part of an interdisciplinary health care team. Culturally competent social work in acute, ambulatory, preventive, long-term, and palliative care settings. Ethical dilemmas in social work in health care. Lecturer - PSYC 220: Introductory Statistics in Psychology (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 16, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Psychology at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach PSYC 220: Introductory Statistics in Psychology. Salary is commensurate with credential and experience. The course teaches basic statistical methods for analysis of data in psychology; descriptive and inferential statistics; hypothesis testing; parametric tests of significance. Introduction to linear regression and correlation; analysis of variance; nonparametric techniques. The requirements will include participation in low-risk psychological experiments or completion of additional short papers.\nTwo hours of lecture Two hours of activities. Lecturer - CHEM 352L: Protein Biochemistry Laboratory (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 14, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach CHEM 352L: Protein Biochemistry Laboratory. The course introduces the theory and practice of modern protein biochemistry. Covers bacterial transformation, antibiotic selection, heterologous protein expression, cell harvesting, cell lysis, centrifugation, affinity chromatography, ion-exchange chromatography, size-exclusion chromatography, hydrophobic-interaction chromatography, dialysis, ultrafiltration, protein precipitation, desalting, bioconjugation, SDS-PAGE, UREA-PAGE, densitometry, fluorescence spectroscopy, western blotting, enzyme activity assays, and in-vitro translation. Lecturer - KINE 181 and 181L: Human Anatomy and Physiology (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 13, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Kinesiology at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for the Fall 2026 semester to teach KINE 181 and 181L: Human Anatomy and Physiology Lecture and Lab. Students enroll in lecture and lab to reinforce knowledge and provide hands on education in Anatomy and Physiology. This is the first course in a two part Anatomy and Physiology Series. An ideal candidate could teach the lecture and all lab courses but multiple instructors may be selected based on availability. More Jobs 123 Hiring Pools Loading... Current Opportunities Position Location Open Date Close Date Lecturer Pool - Computer Science and Information Systems: Cybersecurity AY 2026/27 San Marcos September 01, 2026 May 31, 2027 The Department of Computer Science and Information Systems at California State University San Marcos accepts applications on an on-going basis for our pool of part-time lecturers for Masters in Cybersecurity Program. Applicant pools are used to fill short-term temporary Lecturer positions across our campus with the possibility of rehiring. Appointments may last from one day to a whole semester. This applicant pool may be used to fill vacant positions on an as-needed basis throughout the academic year.  Applications in this pool ad will only be good for the current academic year. This pool will be closed effective May 31st.  If you wish to be considered for the next academic year, you will need to apply to the new pool as it becomes available by June 15th. MBA Research Assistant San Marcos August 05, 2026 May 31, 2027 The CoBA MBA Program is seeking Research Assistants for the 2026-2027 academic year to support several faculty-led research projects in areas related to business, organizations, technology, education, and professional success. Lecturer - SPAN 101: Beginning Spanish I (Fall 2026) San Marcos August 05, 2026 The Modern Language Studies Department at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach SPAN 101: Beginning Spanish I. The course is an introduction to the Spanish language and Spanish-speaking cultures, with emphasis on the development of communicative skills and grammatical structures. Language laboratory practice is a mandatory component of the course. Lecturer AY- KINE 336: Nutrition for Health & Exercise Performance and KINE 416: Global Nutrition and Health Practices (Fall 2026) San Marcos August 04, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Kinesiology at California Stat