ly to the new pool as it becomes available by June 15th. Lecturer - MSW 510: Generalist Practice I: Individuals (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Social Work at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer to teach MSW 510- Generalist Practice I: Individuals. The course addresses generalist social work practice with diverse individuals within a person-in-environment perspective. Emphasizes core social work knowledge, values, and skills within the context of evidence informed engagement, assessment, intervention, and evaluation. Lecturer - ANTH 240: Intro to Biological Anthropology (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Anthropology at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach ANTH-240 Introduction to Biological Anthropology. The course introduces students to the subfield of anthropology that examines human origins, evolution, biological variation, and adaptability. Topics include the basic principles of genetics and inheritance, evolutionary theory, primate biology and behavior, the fossil record of human and nonhuman primates, and contemporary human biological diversity. Lecturer - GES 102: Matter, Molecules, Life, and the Environment II (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture GES 102: Matter, Molecules, Life and the Environment II. The course is the second of a two-semester course consisting of integrated modules covering the areas of matter/energy, molecules, living systems, and environment. These modules will cover major concepts in the physical and biological sciences, emphasizing their application to real-world problems. Concepts covered will include the interactions of matter and energy, laws of motion, atomic structure of matter, structure and properties of molecules, principles of genetics, structure and function of living organisms, evolution, and interactions of organisms with each other and their environment. Includes practical experience in the application of the scientific method through laboratory activities. Lecturer - BIOL 104: Priciples of Biology: Human Emphasis  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 104: Principles of Biology: Human Emphasis. The course teaches the principles of cellular, organismal and population biology with primary representation relating to the human organism. Includes study of cells, tissues, and mammalian organ systems. Lecturer - BIOL 212: Evolution  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 212: Evolution. The course is a consideration of evolution as the unifying concept in biology. Diversity and adaptation of form, function, and behavior of living organisms. Biological, geological, anthropological, and chemical evidence for and mechanisms of evolutionary change, including global pattern of distribution and specialization, mass extinctions, the evolution of race and sex, and the origin of species. Lecturer - BIOL 215: Experimental Design & Statistical Analysis  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 215: Experimental Design and Statistical Analysis. The course teaches the design and analysis of biological surveys and experiments. Includes hypothesis formation, experimental design, statistical analysis, presentation of results, and hands-on experience in design and analysis of biological experiments. Lecturer - BIOL 354: Principles of Ecology  (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 20, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Biological Sciences at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to lecture BIOL 354: Principles of Ecology. The course is a discussion of major concepts in population, community, and evolutionary ecology including population growth and regulation, competition, predation, energetics, adaptations, and diversity. Lecturer - MSW 661: Social Work in Health Care (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 16, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Social Work at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer to teach MSW 661- Social Work in Healthcare. The course covers the roles and responsibilities of social workers as part of an interdisciplinary health care team. Culturally competent social work in acute, ambulatory, preventive, long-term, and palliative care settings. Ethical dilemmas in social work in health care. Lecturer - PSYC 220: Introductory Statistics in Psychology (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 16, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Psychology at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach PSYC 220: Introductory Statistics in Psychology. Salary is commensurate with credential and experience. The course teaches basic statistical methods for analysis of data in psychology; descriptive and inferential statistics; hypothesis testing; parametric tests of significance. Introduction to linear regression and correlation; analysis of variance; nonparametric techniques. The requirements will include participation in low-risk psychological experiments or completion of additional short papers.\nTwo hours of lecture Two hours of activities. Lecturer - CHEM 352L: Protein Biochemistry Laboratory (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 14, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach CHEM 352L: Protein Biochemistry Laboratory. The course introduces the theory and practice of modern protein biochemistry. Covers bacterial transformation, antibiotic selection, heterologous protein expression, cell harvesting, cell lysis, centrifugation, affinity chromatography, ion-exchange chromatography, size-exclusion chromatography, hydrophobic-interaction chromatography, dialysis, ultrafiltration, protein precipitation, desalting, bioconjugation, SDS-PAGE, UREA-PAGE, densitometry, fluorescence spectroscopy, western blotting, enzyme activity assays, and in-vitro translation. Lecturer - KINE 181 and 181L: Human Anatomy and Physiology (Fall 2026) San Marcos July 13, 2026 December 18, 2026 The Department of Kinesiology at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for the Fall 2026 semester to teach KINE 181 and 181L: Human Anatomy and Physiology Lecture and Lab. Students enroll in lecture and lab to reinforce knowledge and provide hands on education in Anatomy and Physiology. This is the first course in a two part Anatomy and Physiology Series. An ideal candidate could teach the lecture and all lab courses but multiple instructors may be selected based on availability. More Jobs 123 Powered by PageUp Job search e.g. \"Director, Technology\" Refine search Work type Instructional Faculty - Temporary/Lecturer 142 Instructional Faculty – Tenured/Tenure-Track 1 Management (MPP) 0 Staff 0 Visiting Faculty 0 Locations Southern California San Marcos 143 Categories Appointment Type At-Will 0 Probationary 0 Temporary 142 Tenured/Tenure-Track 1 Bargaining Unit MPP 0 Unit 3 - CFA - California Faculty Association 143 Unit 4 - APC - Academic Professionals of California 0 Unit 5 - CSUEU - Operations and Support Services 0 Unit 6 - Teamsters Local 2010 0 Unit 7 - CSUEU - Clerical and Administrative Support Services 0 Unit 8 - SUPA - State University Police Association 0 Unit 9 - CSUEU - Technical Support Services 0 Job Search Category/Discipline Administrative 0 Counselor (Non-instructional F