      "title": "CSUSM Recruitment - Details - Lecturer - MUSC 311: Advanced Recording Techniques (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "CSUSM Recruitment - Details - Lecturer - MUSC 311: Advanced Recording Techniques (Fall 2026) skip to main content skip to navigation skip to current link Site Menu Job Opportunities Staff and Management Careers Faculty Careers CSUSM Corporation Careers Student Employment Pay and Benefits Benefits Portal Employment and Compensation About About San Marcos skip to main content skip to section navigation CSUSM Recruitment Job Opportunities Pay and Benefits About Staff and Management Careers Faculty Careers CSUSM Corporation Careers Student Employment Benefits Portal Employment and Compensation About San Marcos CSUSM Recruitment Great Minds Doing Great Work EXISTING APPLICANT LOGIN Lecturer - MUSC 311: Advanced Recording Techniques (Fall 2026) Apply now Job no: 560508 Work type: Instructional Faculty - Temporary/Lecturer Location: San Marcos Categories: Unit 3 - CFA - California Faculty Association, Faculty - Fine/Performing Arts, Temporary, Part Time MUSC 311: Advanced Recording Techniques Position: Lecturer Semester: Fall 2026 Day/Time: Mondays and Wednesdays, from 1:30 to 3:20 p.m. Modality: In-person College: College of Humanities, Arts, behavioral and Social Sciences Department: Music The Department of Music at California State University San Marcos seeks a part-time lecturer for Fall 2026 to teach MUSC 311: Advanced Recording Technology. Course Description: Continuation of the study of recording techniques. Includes advanced use of Pro Tools editing software and WAVES plug-in effects, microphone placement, and recording in both a studio and concert setting. Particular attention to advanced editing, mixing and mastering techniques. Essential Responsibilities: Teach advanced concepts in digital audio recording using Pro Tools Ultimate software and hardware. Instruct students in professional microphone selection, polar patterns, placement techniques, signal flow, cabling, and recording practices. Demonstrate the use of analog and digital mixers, audio interfaces, studio hardware, and outboard equipment. Teach advanced editing, mixing, mastering, and final mix preparation techniques using industry-standard workflows. Provide instruction on Waves plug-ins and other professional audio processing tools. Guide students through hands-on recording sessions, studio projects, and collaborative production exercises. Integrate current industry resources, online tutorials, and professional audio websites into course instruction. Evaluate student performance through practical recording projects, listening exercises, technical demonstrations, and written assessments. Minimum qualifications: A bachelor's degree in music technology, audio engineering, recording arts, music production, or a closely related field; or equivalent professional experience. Demonstrated proficiency with Pro Tools Ultimate. Experience using professional recording studio equipment, microphones, mixers, and digital audio workstations. Knowledge of audio signal flow, recording techniques, mixing, mastering, and audio editing. Ability to teach hands-on technical skills in a collaborative learning environment. Per the California State University’s Out-of-State Employment Policy, the CSU is prohibited from hiring employees to perform CSU-related work outside California. Working in the State of California is a condition of employment. Preferred qualifications: Master of Music or equivalent advanced degree Teaching experience at the college, university, or professional training level. Current professional experience in recording, mixing, mastering, music production, post-production, or live sound. Experience with current plug-ins and other industry-standard audio software. Familiarity with current trends in music production and digital audio technology. Preference will be given to applicants who demonstrate intercultural competence and a commitment to serving our campus community as it relates to teaching and, as applicable, service. Salary commensurate w